bustling movie production company that produced dozens of films and serials starring some of the best-known movie actors of the day. We will study the history of silent film production by exploring Ithaca's dynamic natural and architectural landscape; visiting university special collections that hold related archival materials; watching and discussing silent films; and producing our own Ithaca-inspired short silent films. We will pay particular focus to the aesthetics of film production, including aspects such as costuming, set design, framing, editing, typeface and graphics.\u202f", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-CEL)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "This is a Learning Where You Live course.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "CU", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2797, "crseId": 372031, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "UNILWYL", "catalogNbr": "1156", "titleShort": "Optimize Your 1st Yr Experienc", "titleLong": "Optimizing Your First Year Experience: Queer Identities and Beyond", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 19794, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "07:00PM", "timeEnd": "07:50PM", "startDt": "08/26/2021", "endDt": "12/07/2021", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "cm879", "firstName": "Claire", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Menard"}], "pattern": "M", "facilityDescr": "Mews Residence Hall 146", "bldgDescr": "Mews Residence Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "MEW146", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This is a Learning Where You Live course. Priority given to Loving House in-house residents."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "08/26/2021", "endDt": "12/18/2021", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 1, "unitsMaximum": 1, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "SUS", "gradingBasisShort": "Sat/Unsat", "gradingBasisLong": "Satisfactory/Unsatisfactory", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "08/26/2021", "sessionEndDt": "12/18/2021", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "Optimizing Your First Year Experience: Queer Identities &amp; Beyond is designed to provide community, education and supportive matriculation for our LGBTQIA+ and ally identifying students at Cornell University who are connected to Loving House in their first year. This course will provide support to students as they navigate the ambiguity that arises from their transition to college. This course will promote and encourage self-exploration of your queer identities, ways to be successful at Cornell and beyond while keeping in mind the importance your identity plays into your experience as a student and as a global citizen. This course will look at the historical context of the LGBTQIA+ community and how that interacts with the queer experience.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "This is a Learning Where You Live course.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null,